From: Simon Spitzer <simon.spitzer@live.de>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 07:31:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Prepend https:// to URL fields without scheme

Entering e.g. "www.example.com" into a URL field was rejected by the
browser's built-in validation. Now "https://" is prepended automatically
when the field is changed or the form is submitted via enter. Values which
already contain a scheme (e.g. mailto: or tel:) are left unchanged.

Fixes #3339

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
